Hi, I browsed the LB codebase for use of thread local storage, and i find one usage instance, which is that the Boost thread local storage abstraction is used to carry a PRNG, here:

.//libbitcoin/src/utility/pseudo_random.cpp:    static boost::thread_specific_ptr<std::mt19937> twister(deleter);

Just curious why is this done, the OS for instance offers a random function?

